{:adr-id "2608030000"
 :title "cloud-itonami-isic-0721 — Uranium and Thorium Ore Mining Operations Coordination"
 :date "2026-07-15"
 :author "Cloud Itonami Contributors"
 :status :accepted
 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 0721 (Mining of uranium and thorium ores) had no prior
  actor implementation -- the registry entry pointed at a placeholder
  repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-B0721) that was never created. This
  session independently verified the live registry against a fresh
  clone before proceeding: {:id \"0721\" :name \"Mining of uranium and
  thorium ores\" :maturity :spec ...} -- confirmed the id/name match.
  Scope note: a legitimate civilian nuclear-fuel-cycle raw-material
  mining classification, radiation-safety-regulated, NOT
  weapons-related, distinct from the deliberately-excluded ISIC
  2520/3040 weapons classes. Fresh, from-scratch scaffold, built as
  part of a smaller, carefully verified batch after an earlier
  18-agent haiku batch's 61% defect rate. Module shape mirrors sibling
  cloud-itonami-isic-0893 (Extraction of salt)'s verified module
  shape, domain-adapted for uranium/thorium mining: ISIC 0721 covers
  both conventional open-pit/underground mining and in-situ recovery
  (ISR) wellfields, and both uranium and thorium ores, so the demo
  site directory seeds one conventional-uranium site, one
  ISR-uranium site, and one thorium site (unverified permit)
  deliberately."
 :decision
 {:scope-boundary
  "Coordination-only actor. Closed four-op allowlist, all :effect
   :propose: log-extraction-record, schedule-mining-operation,
   flag-radiological-concern (always escalates), coordinate-shipment
   (always escalates -- IAEA-safeguarded material, distinct from most
   sibling shipment ops in this fleet which do not always escalate).
   An op outside this set is the same failure mode as forbidden-scope
   content, not a separate carve-out."
  :governor-rules
  "Three HARD, permanent, un-overridable checks: (1)
   mine-site-unverified -- target site must be independently
   :registered?/:permit-verified? in the store, never trusted from the
   proposal's own claim; (2) effect-not-propose -- any :effect other
   than :propose is a claim to directly actuate outside governance;
   (3) scope-exclusion -- any proposal (any op) touching
   mining-equipment-control (conventional: drill-and-blast/haul-truck-
   dispatch/shaft-hoist-control/continuous-miner; ISR: wellfield-
   injection/wellfield-extraction-well/ion-exchange-circuit-control/
   elution-circuit-control; shared mill circuit: leach-circuit-
   control/solvent-extraction-control/yellowcake-precipitation/
   calciner-control/mill-circuit-control) or radiation-safety
   (-certification-authority) territory (exposure-limit-override,
   tailings-containment-override, ventilation/shielding-control-
   decision, radioactive-material license issuance, license
   suspension, compliance enforcement), evaluated unconditionally via
   a lower-cased EN+JA substring scan of the proposal's own content.
   Exposure/tailings-containment exclusion terms are deliberately
   qualified (override / control decision) so legitimate
   flag-radiological-concern observations are never self-blocked --
   exercised directly by
   legitimate-radiological-concern-flag-is-not-scope-excluded.
   Escalation (soft): flag-radiological-concern always,
   coordinate-shipment always (IAEA safeguards), low confidence
   (<0.6). uraniumops.phase independently agrees -- neither op ever
   auto-commits at any phase."
  :module-shape
  "uraniumops.store (MemStore, string-keyed site directory seeded with
   a conventional uranium mine, an ISR uranium wellfield, and an
   unverified-permit thorium mine), advisor (UraniumOpsAdvisor, mock +
   real-LLM seam via langchain.model, plus an :out-of-scope? test
   hook), governor (UraniumThoriumMiningGovernor), phase (0->3
   rollout), operation (langgraph-clj StateGraph), sim (demo driver)."}
 :consequences
